# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: intern names in deduplicated files
#
# Every item name was written twice: in the item_names table and in the item's ItemMeta (chelis-deep:
# 26 MB of item_names, a seventh of the file, mostly the generic arguments of Instantiated path
# elements of monomorphized copies). When values are deduplicated, names are now interned like spans:
# the first occurrence of each distinct name is {"Def": [id, path]}, later ones are the id alone.
# item_names comes first, so item metas refer to its names by id. Rust deserialization and charon-ml
# give back the same names; no field or type changes.
#
# The span table of the dedup state becomes a generic Interner used for spans and names; generate-ml
# decodes names with a hand-written interned_name_of_json and treats names as order-dependent values
# in opaque fields.

